= Air Travel Guidelines

== Commercial Air Travel Principles

Air travel constitutes one of the largest single budget lines across Noice & Toit LLP. Flying is often necessary to conduct client discovery sessions, deliver high-stakes litigation arguments, or participate in executive steering committees across continents.

Our policy balances employee health, safety, and productivity with our partnership's duty to manage travel costs responsibly. All airline bookings must be made through our designated corporate travel management portal (accessible via the Noice & Toit intranet), which provides direct corporate discounts, duty of care tracking, and centralized billing.

== Advance Booking Expectations

Airfares fluctuate wildly based on capacity, seasonality, and booking lead time. Last-minute bookings represent an unnecessary drain on partnership resources.

#card-do("Book flights at least 14 days in advance")[
  Plan your travel early and reserve flights at least fourteen calendar days prior to domestic travel and twenty-one calendar days prior to international flights. Advance booking ensures access to competitive economy inventory.
]

#card-dont("Delay booking until the departure window")[
  Do not delay booking flights until the week of departure. Bookings made inside seven days of travel require written justification explaining why client circumstances or project milestones prevented earlier reservation.
]

== Cabin Class Policies and Travel Thresholds

Our cabin class policy is governed by scheduled flight duration and business requirements.

=== Standard Economy Class
Economy class is mandatory for all domestic flights and short-haul international flights where scheduled flight duration is under eight (8) consecutive hours in the air. Travelers should select standard non-refundable fares.

=== Premium Economy
Premium Economy is permitted for flights with scheduled flight times between six (6) and eight (8) continuous hours, provided written pre-approval has been granted by your Department Director or Practice Leader.

=== Long-Haul Business Class Exception
Business class travel is reserved exclusively for long-haul intercontinental flights meeting strict criteria:
- The non-stop flight duration must strictly exceed eight (8) continuous hours, or
- The traveler must conduct a critical, documented client presentation or trial hearing within four (4) hours of scheduled flight arrival without an intervening rest night.

#card-dont("Book First Class under any circumstance")[
  First Class travel (transcontinental flagship or international long-haul) is strictly prohibited across all routes, regardless of flight length, seniority, or client billing status. Any employee booking First Class will have the entire ticket value rejected or clawed back.
]

#card-do("Use approved travel booking channels")[
  Book all flights through our corporate travel portal or dedicated travel desk. Bookings made directly on third-party airline websites are difficult to track during emergencies and may not receive corporate flight change waivers.
]

== Baggage Allowances and Incidental Flight Costs

Airlines frequently add unbundled fees for baggage handling, seat assignments, and boarding privileges.

#card-do("Expense one standard checked bag")[
  The firm reimburses one standard checked baggage fee per traveler for business trips extending beyond two days. Keep the itemized baggage payment receipt or ensure the baggage charge appears as a separate line item on your e-ticket invoice.
]

#card-dont("Expense seat selection or priority perks")[
  Do not expense extra-legroom seats, priority boarding passes, airport express security lane passes, or airport lounge day-passes. If an employee chooses to purchase enhanced seating for personal comfort, they must pay for that upgrade out of personal funds.
]

== Flight Changes, Delays, and Unused Tickets

Business schedules change rapidly, but ticket alterations must be managed with care:
- *Voluntary Ticket Changes*: Changing a flight due to changing personal preferences is non-reimbursable. Changes prompted by shifting client meetings or court dates are fully reimbursable, provided the client code is cited.
- *Unused Ticket Credits*: When a non-refundable flight is canceled for business reasons, the resulting airline credit belongs to Noice & Toit LLP. The employee must track this credit and apply it to their next business journey.
- *Flight Disruption Assistance*: In the event of severe weather cancellations or carrier delays, contact the 24/7 Noice & Toit Travel Assistance Desk for rebooking support.

== In-Flight Connectivity and Wi-Fi

Onboard Wi-Fi is reimbursable only when the flight duration exceeds three hours and active connectivity is required to complete urgent, time-sensitive client deliverables. General browsing, entertainment streaming, and casual messaging do not qualify for reimbursement.

== Sustainable Aviation and Carbon Offsetting

Noice & Toit LLP is committed to reducing corporate carbon emissions by 30% by 2030. When planning travel:
- Assess whether high-definition video conferencing can achieve the same client outcome without travel.
- For regional European and US Northeast corridor routes, evaluate high-speed rail options before booking flights.
- All corporate flight bookings automatically include mandatory verified carbon offset contributions funded centrally by the firm.

== Frequently Asked Questions

*Q: Can I keep frequent flyer miles and airline status points earned on business flights?*\
A: Yes. Employees may retain airline frequent flyer miles and loyalty perks for personal use. However, you may not select a more expensive flight, inconvenient layover, or non-preferred carrier simply to earn loyalty points on a specific airline.

*Q: What if I want to fly business class on a five-hour flight and pay the difference myself?*\
A: You may upgrade your seat using personal funds or personal frequent flyer miles. If booking through our corporate portal, request a split-billing invoice showing the baseline economy fare paid by the firm and the upgrade delta paid directly on your personal credit card.

*Q: What happens if an airline involuntarily bumps me and offers cash compensation?*\
A: Involuntary or voluntary denied-boarding compensation belongs to the traveler as compensation for personal inconvenience, provided accepting the offer does not cause the traveler to miss client commitments or incur extra hotel costs for the firm.
